Latest fix: bookmark placement drag and docking

- Reused the existing latest-fix directory instead of adding a new sibling fix; removed the older duplicate fix directory.
- Enabled dragging from the bookmark header in vertical docked sidebars as well as Windowed overlays.
- In icon-only mode, centered the expand/collapse button and added a separated divider/grip below it as the drag target.
- During a drag, the bookmark drawer and overlay become a bookmark-shaped icon that follows the pointer, with the page shielded to prevent the prohibited/stop cursor.
- Translucent previews show both the bookmark bar and the panel destination.
- Top/bottom docking on a vertical docked sidebar converts bookmarks to a horizontal bar and shortens the sidebar to reserve space; left/right drops return to the usual adjacent drawer without adding vertical spacing.
- Horizontal bars have a grip so they can be dragged back beside the overlay.
- Preserved floating-window offset behavior and constrained panel height so a bottom bar stays within the viewport.
- Included every current root extension file in the nested folder; content.js, defaults.js, README.md, tp-bookmarks.js, and tp-css.js are the modified copies. Backup is excluded.
